{"id":"EUVD-2026-133254","enisaUuid":"735207c1-617b-33bb-80b7-8cdd1c3a135f","description":"XO (Xen Orchestra) is a solution to visualize, manage, backup and delegate your XCP-ng (or XenServer) infrastructure. Prior to 6.9.2 and 6.10.1, REST cookie parsing turns authenticationToken\u003dj:%7B%7D into {}. REST authentication passes that object to the XO token provider without requiring a string. The token collection treats {} as an unfiltered lookup and returns its first token; the provider authenticates as that token\u0027s owner if it is unexpired. The authenticated /rest/v0/users/me/authentication_tokens route then returns reusable login token IDs. This vulnerability is actively exploited in the wild. This vulnerability is fixed in 6.9.2 and 6.10.1.","datePublished":"Nov 23, 2026, 5:07:16 PM","dateUpdated":"Nov 23, 2026, 6:25:46 PM","baseScore":9.8,"baseScoreVersion":"3.1","baseScoreVector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","references":"https://github.com/vatesfr/xen-orchestra/security/advisories/GHSA-2r3w-c2vx-fv5g\nhttps://github.com/vatesfr/xen-orchestra/pull/10748\nhttps://github.com/vatesfr/xen-orchestra/commit/50166fe3a49c02069d35ba9046ca4a1f77f4e11d\nhttps://docs.vates.tech/security-advisories/advisories/2026/vates-sa-2026-062\n","aliases":"CVE-2026-133469\nGHSA-2r3w-c2vx-fv5g\n","assigner":"GitHub_M","epss":0.0,"enisaIdProduct":[{"id":"33cb09e8-6ae1-3889-a35e-061ff21dc22c","product":{"name":"xen-orchestra","vendor":{"name":"vatesfr"}},"product_version":"\u003c 6.9.2"},{"id":"6b9c8a00-539f-3fea-8b8a-48efe15a51a0","product":{"name":"xen-orchestra","vendor":{"name":"vatesfr"}},"product_version":"6.10.0, \u003c 6.10.1"},{"id":"8748ce1b-9da7-3510-ace4-648f02aa6599","product":{"name":"xo-server","vendor":{"name":"xen-orchestra"}},"product_version":"\u003c 5.211.2"},{"id":"ea5dfe79-ab1b-32ad-b2f5-50ed87ba9835","product":{"name":"xo-server","vendor":{"name":"xen-orchestra"}},"product_version":"5.213.0, \u003c 5.213.1"}],"enisaIdVendor":[{"id":"436fe0c